# Caddy — OPT-IN local HTTPS / HTTP-2 edge (mirror of docker/Caddyfile).
#
# This is the opt-in TLS profile from renderer-stage0-plan.md §0.5. The default
# dev edge stays plain HTTP/1.1 on :8080 (docker/Caddyfile, byte-unchanged); this
# file is loaded ONLY via the docker-compose.https.yml override and serves the
# SAME three handles over https://localhost with HTTP/2.
#
# It expects a locally-trusted cert pair at the stable paths /certs/localhost.pem
# and /certs/localhost-key.pem, mounted from ./docker/certs (see docs/https-local.md
# for the one-time mkcert step). No domain and no purchased certificate are needed
# locally — a domain + Caddy automatic HTTPS is only for public deployments.
#
# The datasets file server (immutable Cache-Control from {DATA_ROOT}/datasets/,
# D-30) and the /api reverse-proxy to uvicorn are now SHARED with the other edge
# profiles via docker/Caddyfile.edge-snippets (imported below, T2-76), so they no
# longer need hand-syncing; only the site address, the TLS directive, and the
# catch-all to the vite dev server are profile-specific here.
{
	# Opt-in TLS edge. auto_https is left at its default here because we supply an
	# explicit cert via the `tls` directive below; admin off matches the base edge.
	admin off
}

# Load the shared edge snippet definitions (datasets_edge, api_edge) so the site
# block below can `import` them by name (T2-76). Mounted alongside this Caddyfile.
import Caddyfile.edge-snippets

# The base compose file maps host :8080 -> container :80 and an override cannot
# UN-map an inherited port. Without an explicit http:// site, Caddy's automatic
# HTTP->HTTPS redirect would point at https://localhost (no port — its https_port
# is the in-container 443), which is unreachable from the host; anyone hitting the
# familiar dev URL http://localhost:8080 would get a dead redirect. Send them to
# the real external HTTPS edge instead (transcribed from Caddyfile.prod, PR #81 —
# T2-51).
http://localhost {
	redir https://localhost:8443{uri}
}

https://localhost {
	# Locally-trusted cert pair issued by mkcert on the HOST (one-time
	# `mkcert -install` + `mkcert localhost 127.0.0.1 ::1`), placed at these
	# stable filenames under ./docker/certs. See docs/https-local.md.
	tls /certs/localhost.pem /certs/localhost-key.pem

	# Static versioned dataset assets (D-30) and the /api reverse-proxy are shared,
	# byte-identical across all three edge profiles — imported from the shared
	# snippet file so an edge change lands once (T2-76). See docker/Caddyfile.edge-snippets.
	import datasets_edge
	import api_edge

	# Dev convenience: the app shell -> the vite dev server.
	handle {
		reverse_proxy frontend:5173
	}
}
